"""Add Figure 51 (fig-depth-routing) after Figure 50 and bump the data versions (owner popup 2026-11-05). Argon draft, corrected by hand: mHC does not state its size, the 48-layer value was measured before the prediction, two of the three learned runs at 48 layers are on the older code. Nothing is written if an assert fails."""
import html, json
P = "/scratch/gpfs/GROUP/USER/tmp/plc_site_wt/exps/per-layer-contribution.html"
s = open(P, encoding="utf-8").read()
e = lambda t: html.escape(t, quote=True)
d = json.load(open("/scratch/gpfs/GROUP/USER/tmp/pls_hcid/caps_1105c_out.json"))
EN = ("Papers on Hyper-Connections, mHC and AttnRes report that removing learned routing raises the loss by 0.012–0.022, at 16 layers where they state the size. At 48 layers we find that fixing the mixing to the identity lowers the loss. We ask whether depth explains the difference. We train Hyper-Connections at 12 and 24 layers on the same code and the same budget, with full learned mixing and with identity mixing. At 48 layers we use every run, and two of the three with full learned mixing are on the older code. Read and write stay learned in both models, so this change removes only the mixing. The left panel plots the final held-out loss of the last layer. Dots show individual runs and lines join their means. Pre-LN is the model with one path. The right panel plots identity mixing minus full learned mixing at each evaluation step, so a positive value means learned mixing helps. At the end the value is +0.016 nats at 12 layers, −0.020 at 24 and −0.056 at 48. Before the 12- and 24-layer runs started, we predicted at least +0.01 and about 0 for them. The two shallower values sit below 0.03 nats, so we read them as no effect larger than that. The 12-layer value has the same size as the papers' reports, whose runs use other training recipes and, where stated, far more tokens. Two seeds of Hyper-Connections at 48 layers differ by 0.041 nats, and each shallower depth has one pair of runs. Only the change from 12 to 48 layers, 0.072 nats, exceeds the difference between seeds. The three depths keep the same order at all five evaluation steps, and each depth ends lower than at step 1,000. Pre-LN stays above identity mixing by 0.061, 0.085 and 0.090 nats at the three depths. Its 12- and 24-layer runs use the older code, which moves Pre-LN by 0.006 nats at 48 layers. An older-code run of Hyper-Connections reaches 3.764 nats at 12 layers and 3.704 at 24, which would put the differences at +0.020 and −0.044. One more 48-layer run with learned mixing overflowed from step 4,408, so we leave it out.")
ZH = ("Hyper-Connections、mHC 和 AttnRes 的论文报告，去掉学到的路由会让损失升高 0.012–0.022，标明规模的都是 16 层。我们在 48 层模型里发现，把混合固定为单位混合反而会降低损失。我们检验深度能否解释这一差异。我们用同一套代码和相同预算在 12 层和 24 层上训练 Hyper-Connections，分别采用完整学到混合和单位混合。48 层用全部运行，其中完整学到混合的三次运行有两次在旧代码上。两个模型都保留学到的读写，所以这一改动只去掉混合。左图画最后一层的最终留出损失。圆点代表单次运行，折线连接均值。Pre-LN 是单通路模型。右图画每个评估步上单位混合减去完整学到混合的差值，所以正值代表学到混合有益。训练结束时，这一差值在 12 层为 +0.016 nats，在 24 层为 −0.020，在 48 层为 −0.056。在 12 层和 24 层运行启动前，我们预测这两个值至少为 +0.01 和接近 0。两个较浅深度的数值都低于 0.03 nats，所以我们认为那里不存在超过这一幅度的效应。12 层的数值与论文报告的大小相同，而论文用的是其他训练配方，标明预算的都用了多得多的 token。48 层 Hyper-Connections 的两个种子相差 0.041 nats，两个较浅深度则各有一对运行。所以只有从 12 层到 48 层的 0.072 nats 变化量超过了种子间的差距。三个深度在全部 5 个评估步上保持同一顺序，而且每个深度在终点都比第 1,000 步时更低。在三个深度上，Pre-LN 的损失始终比单位混合高 0.061、0.085 和 0.090 nats。它的 12 层和 24 层运行使用旧代码，而旧代码在 48 层上使 Pre-LN 偏移 0.006 nats。旧代码下的 Hyper-Connections 在 12 层是 3.764 nats，在 24 层是 3.704，换算出的差值为 +0.020 和 −0.044。另有一次带学到混合的 48 层运行从第 4,408 步起溢出，所以我们排除它。")
fig = ('\n  <figure class="viz" data-more-en="' + e(EN) + '"\n    data-more-zh="' + e(ZH) + '" id="fig-depth-routing" data-src=""\n'
       '    data-title-en="Learned mixing and extra paths at 12, 24 and 48 layers" data-title-zh="学到的混合和额外通路，12、24、48 层"\n'
       '    data-cap-en="' + e(d["cap_en"]) + '"\n    data-cap-zh="' + e(d["cap_zh"]) + '"></figure>')
assert 'id="fig-depth-routing"' not in s
i = s.index('id="fig-sep-probes"'); b = s.index('</figure>', i) + len('</figure>')
s = s[:b] + fig + s[b:]
for a, c in (("plc-figures.js?v=140", "plc-figures.js?v=141"), ("plc-record.js?v=112", "plc-record.js?v=113")):
    assert s.count(a) == 1, a
    s = s.replace(a, c)
